{
 "description": "How the fused profile matches the radar's own trackers to object-list tracks. ACC target: position cost = |dRel - x| / max(12 m, 0.25 x) + |yRel - y| / 0.5 m with x the 0.025 m ACC distance and y its 0.01 m lateral (earlier: a coarse 5-bit view of the distance and a fixed 12 m scale). Summaries (0x192 / 0x194): attached to the track at the summary position, range within 15 % and lateral within 1 m (earlier: range plus agreement of the object-list speed with the summary slope within 1.5 m/s). Emulations replay the interface rules with their state over the logged frames; set 1 = 700 one-minute segments, set 2 = 114 segments of other drives. Replays: 34 drives through openpilot's radard and planner, each step against the previous one under limits fixed before the run.",
